--- !u!1 &73960023
GameObject:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  serializedVersion: 6
  m_Component:
  - component: {fileID: 73960026}
  - component: {fileID: 73960025}
  - component: {fileID: 73960024}
  m_Layer: 0
  m_Name: Dialogue_Beat0_Briefing
  m_TagString: Untagged
  m_Icon: {fileID: 0}
  m_NavMeshLayer: 0
  m_StaticEditorFlags: 0
  m_IsActive: 1
--- !u!114 &73960024
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 73960023}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 51bf743a7b9a61e409329faa416e2f81, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Ronin7.World::Ronin7.World.Story.DialoguePlayer
  lines:
  - speaker: Morrigan
    text: First thing the bench tells me, and you're not going to like it. Whoever
      cut your leash knew this firmware better than the people who shipped it. Every
      block they touched, they touched in the right order. No scavenger gets that
      lucky. Somebody who builds leashes for a living did this. An insider.
    seconds: 19
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: d2b3e2db87e0f2541af790165432683e, type: 3}
  - speaker: Mera Voss
    text: An insider who breaks the Program's own leashes. That's either the best
      news we've had or a very well-built trap. From here I can't tell which.
    seconds: 9
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 967c0b508d7f96a4994e7480592dd457, type: 3}
  - speaker: Morrigan
    text: Which is why we leave the insider for now and go after the papers that
      would name them. There's a collector who trades them. Operative records, the
      real ones, the erased ones, bought and hoarded off every black market that
      handles dead Program assets. One name keeps surfacing under all of it. Coral
      Vex.
    seconds: 18
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 13976607ac8cf2343aeff258f73bca59, type: 3}
  - speaker: Resh
    text: Vex. Yeah. I've heard salvagers say the name in a low voice, like you'd
      talk about a place you don't loot. She runs a reliquary out in the dead lanes,
      an old records-barge she gutted and made her own. Buys the paper of dead operatives
      and never sells a sheet of it back. Hoards it. Nobody's worked out why.
    seconds: 18
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: e20d47e9debdfa446906e57dd4e4a36e, type: 3}
  - speaker: Iris
    text: A collector who keeps records of the erased and won't trade them. That's
      not about money. It's a reason. Nobody hoards the dead for profit. You hoard
      them because somebody has to remember. I want to know who she's remembering.
    seconds: 14
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 93b008975f974f2478f331d1bff92955, type: 3}
  - speaker: Kessler
    text: And I want to know which she is before we knock. Mera's right. You can't
      tell a friend from a hunter on paper.
    seconds: 13
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 58f17acec317b3548963c5a225641cd6, type: 3}
  - speaker: Mera Voss
    text: You tell them apart inside. An ally lets you leave. A hunter lets you get
      in deep first. So we go in expecting both and we keep a route back to the hull.
    seconds: 11
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 149779e4d5ad58340b822adacc06a1fe, type: 3}
  - speaker: Mira
    text: Is that the thing in his head?
    seconds: 2
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7f5bbb5310f5e544b807dc956a031f1e, type: 3}
  - speaker: Morrigan
    text: It's the thing they put in his head, and the thing somebody else took out
      for him. Both. That's what doesn't fit, little one. The Program builds these
      to never come off. His came off clean. Someone wanted it to.
    seconds: 14
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 80324301de92a3a45833ae2b899b9829, type: 3}
  - speaker: Echo
    text: Cipher, I don't love walking toward somebody who keeps shadows for a living.
      A woman with a barge full of the erased is exactly who I'd be afraid of, if
      I were the kind of thing that could be shelved. Which I am.
    seconds: 16
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 54b1c8118d8c8b84b8b2eb6a7831cfae, type: 3}
  - speaker: Ronin-7
    text: Then we go meet the one person who might know what they did with the rest
      of you.
    seconds: 6
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 4a5496f7f8043794b8b1e5c64f48444f, type: 3}
  - speaker: Ronin-7
    text: Somebody opened my door. I'm done not knowing who stands on the other side
      of it. Plot the reliquary.
    seconds: 8
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7828b3b254d72b544a6d6ad4a3276d64, type: 3}
  - speaker: Kessler
    text: All right. Dead lanes, slow approach, no dock. We put you on the hull and
      we hold off it, comm open, route home kept clear. Same as the mountain. You
      go in, Cipher, you find out which she is, you come back.
    seconds: 14
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: c983b395170183c428c492ed5e8bb960, type: 3}
  textMesh: {fileID: 1514047102}
  panelRoot: {fileID: 1294230452}
  audioSource: {fileID: 73960025}
  billboardToCamera: 1
  playOnStart: 0
  followDistance: 1.5
  followVerticalOffset: -0.55
  followLerp: 12
  maxCharsPerLine: 36
  autoAdvanceBeat: 0.45
  advanceAction: {fileID: -3790664182463143341, guid: d5a2441a867c2484c888f3631c932d48, type: 3}
