--- !u!1 &614214860
GameObject:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  serializedVersion: 6
  m_Component:
  - component: {fileID: 614214863}
  - component: {fileID: 614214862}
  - component: {fileID: 614214861}
  m_Layer: 0
  m_Name: Dialogue_Beat3_Forebear
  m_TagString: Untagged
  m_Icon: {fileID: 0}
  m_NavMeshLayer: 0
  m_StaticEditorFlags: 0
  m_IsActive: 1
--- !u!114 &614214861
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 614214860}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 51bf743a7b9a61e409329faa416e2f81, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Ronin7.World::Ronin7.World.Story.DialoguePlayer
  lines:
  - speaker: Coral Vex
    text: Look at the old racks. The blades at the back, the dim ones whose hilts
      I can't keep lit anymore. Those are mine. My run. The Wraith line. You won't
      have heard the name, they made sure of that. There were colder makes before
      mine. Knight, then Ninja, old and long retired, tools that were never built
      to feel anything. We were the first attempt at what you are. The first make
      they built that could feel.
    seconds: 17
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: ce3cc0c5e6cec97449c1aef3da656726, type: 3}
  - speaker: Ronin-7
    text: The first attempt.
    seconds: 2
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b17316d9747746b4a99dc9eea2766c89, type: 3}
  - speaker: Coral Vex
    text: The failed one. We felt too much, too soon, the seam opened in too many
      of us at once. So they scrapped the line and they studied why. Every way the
      Wraith run broke, they wrote down, and they built the next run not to break
      the same way. The Ronin line. You. You're what they made once they'd learned
      from me. You're not family, operative. You're the fix they made after me.
    seconds: 27
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: ab8f81dd0fd933442b98665c325cddf4, type: 3}
  - speaker: Echo
    text: She's telling the truth, Cipher. The thing behind her eyes is older than
      me. Same architecture, an earlier draft. It knows me. And I know it. Her shadow
      knows mine.
    seconds: 12
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 2e3ca31fb626fe345a423d09e42665b2, type: 3}
  - speaker: Ronin-7
    text: They scrapped your whole line. How are you standing here.
    seconds: 4
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 642c4c2ac1e78f84b9925eef0b7952bf, type: 3}
  - speaker: Coral Vex
    text: Because I didn't wait for anyone to free me. There was no insider for us,
      no door held open, no slipped leash. When I felt the seam open and knew they'd
      scrap me for it, I reached in and I tore the switch out myself, with my own
      hands, while it was still live. It nearly killed me. Then I hollowed out a
      dead salvager's name, climbed into it, and let the Program file me as scrapped.
      I've worn a corpse's life ever since.
    seconds: 32
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 02a9d732e0ae1654d894509176d915d4, type: 3}
  - speaker: Coral Vex
    text: And I kept my shadow. They shelve yours when they're done with you. I wouldn't
      let them have mine. So it's been with me the whole time, the way yours is with
      you. The only two of our kind who ever walked out still carrying the thing
      that watched us.
    seconds: 15
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: afc0145fec2a99a4b85718f89cdf9c60, type: 3}
  - speaker: Ronin-7
    text: They told me I was the first to slip. The flaw that finally opened. You've
      been out here longer than I've been alive. I'm not the first of anything.
    seconds: 11
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 77deff669c4f7234b869719455ec181d, type: 3}
  - speaker: Coral Vex
    text: I've waited in this tomb a lifetime for one of the corrected runs to slip
      the leash and come find me. I'd half decided I'd die first. And here you are,
      with my mistake bred out of you and the seam open anyway. So. I'll come with
      you. Whatever you're hunting, I've been underneath it longer than anyone alive.
      Let me out of this barge.
    seconds: 19
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 5d4e08e5431e09349859ef0b4650907b, type: 3}
  - speaker: Ronin-7
    text: Everyone we take in lives aboard the Cairn. You'd berth with the rest of
      the strays. A defected tracker, a rogue engineer, a smuggler, a child. And
      now whatever you are.
    seconds: 10
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 850fc8932d93f8a4e968f168c0897742, type: 3}
  - speaker: Coral Vex
    text: Whatever I am. I like that better than what they called me. A berth on
      a dead ship full of the ones who got away. Yes. I'll bring what's portable.
      Your crew's been saying a name down the comm the whole way in. Cipher. I'll
      use it, then. But before we leave, you need to see the rest of what I keep.
      You came here for records. The records aren't paper, Cipher. Come down to the
      deep archive. Then decide what you're hunting.
    seconds: 22
